      "lyrics": "Verse 1\n\nWe rolled out of Dayton with the backseat torn,\nFour broke believers in the blue before dawn,\nKick drum rattlin\u2019 with the jack and the spare,\nA map full of circles and a prayer in the air.\n\nTruck stop coffee and a cigarette moon,\nBathroom mirror says we\u2019ll be home soon,\nBut home\u2019s gettin\u2019 smaller in the rearview glass,\nWe\u2019re chasin\u2019 tomorrow with our foot on the gas.\n\nPre-Chorus\n\nEvery mile is a scar on the chrome,\nEvery song makes the dark less alone,\nWhen the wheels start whinin\u2019 and the night gets mean,\nWe keep burnin\u2019 like gasoline.\n\nChorus\n\nIn a van full of dreams, on a sunrise highway,\nSingin\u2019 whoa-oh-oh, we\u2019re gonna get there someday,\nWith a stack of cassette tapes and our hearts on fire,\nLivin\u2019 on nothin\u2019 but a six-string desire.\n\nIn a van full of dreams, we\u2019re battered but unbroken,\nEvery empty room hears the words we\u2019ve spoken,\nTill the whole world screams what we already know,\nWe were born to run, born to rock, born to roll.\n\nVerse 2\n\nWe played to thirteen in a border-town bar,\nGot paid in quarters and a warm PBR,\nJohnny\u2019s got a postcard from the girl he left,\nSleeps with her picture on a Marshall head.\n\nMotel sign buzzin\u2019 like a neon ghost,\nTwo beds for five on the Oklahoma coast,\nWe laugh till we\u2019re cryin\u2019 on the carpet floor,\nThen pack up our thunder and we beg for more.\n\nPre-Chorus\n\nEvery friend is a flame in the cold,\nEvery chord is a hand we can hold,\nWhen the highway\u2019s hungry and the money\u2019s gone,\nWe hit the first note and we carry on.\n\nChorus\n\nIn a van full of dreams, on a sunrise highway,\nSingin\u2019 whoa-oh-oh, we\u2019re gonna get there someday,\nWith a stack of cassette tapes and our hearts on fire,\nLivin\u2019 on nothin\u2019 but a six-string desire.\n\nIn a van full of dreams, we\u2019re battered but unbroken,\nEvery empty room hears the words we\u2019ve spoken,\nTill the whole world screams what we already know,\nWe were born to run, born to rock, born to roll.\n\nBridge\n\nSometimes I miss the porch light glow,\nMama callin\u2019 from the kitchen window,\nFriday nights and the county fair,\nThe smell of rain in the summer air.\n\nBut I look to my left, see my brothers bleedin\u2019 hope,\nHands on the wheel at the end of the rope,\nWe ain\u2019t got silver, we ain\u2019t got gold,\nBut we got each other and a dream to hold.\n\nFinal Chorus\n\nIn a van full of dreams, on a sunrise highway,\nSingin\u2019 whoa-oh-oh, we\u2019re gonna get there someday,\nWith a stack of cassette tapes and our hearts on fire,\nLivin\u2019 on nothin\u2019 but a six-string desire.\n\nIn a van full of dreams, we\u2019re battered but unbroken,\nEvery empty room hears the words we\u2019ve spoken,\nTill the whole world screams what we already know,\nWe were born to run, born to rock, born to roll.\n\nIn a van full of dreams, under red sky thunder,\nWe\u2019re a long way from home but we\u2019re not goin\u2019 under,\nRaise your hands to the dawn, let the headlights gleam,\nWe\u2019re alive, we\u2019re together, in a van full of dreams.\n\nOutro\n\nWhoa-oh-oh, roll on,\nWhoa-oh-oh, hold on,\nTruck stop saints and motel signs,\nCassette hearts and highway lines.\n\nWhoa-oh-oh, roll on,\nWhoa-oh-oh, hold on,\nTill the last star fades in the morning beams,\nWe\u2019ll be ridin\u2019 forever in a van full of dreams.",
