ur porch in the pouring rain\nBeg you to love me back again\n\nBut time\u2019s a thief in a leather vest\nIt steals the gold and it leaves the rest\nA ring of dust where the diamond shone\nA love song playing to an empty home\n\nFinal Chorus\nPhotograph promises, shaking in my hand\nTwo scared hearts with no second chance\nI wrote forever like the word was true\nBut forever ain\u2019t strong when it\u2019s missing you\nPhotograph promises, beautiful and torn\nA summer kiss and a winter storm\nIf you ever wonder what you meant to me\nYou were the girl in every song I sing\n\nOutro\nI keep your picture in my coat at night\nClose to my heart under neon lights\nAnd when the crowd fades, I whisper through\nEvery photograph promise still belongs to you",
